You are implementing a Blazor Web App for a logistics company that tracks shipments. The project has already been scaffolded at:
- Server project: /tmp/sv-ef500695b1e6440a934dab6536027696/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/
- Client project: /tmp/sv-ef500695b1e6440a934dab6536027696/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/

The project uses Interactive Auto, Global mode with Individual authentication (ASP.NET Core Identity, SQLite).

## What to implement

### 1. Remove template defaults
Delete these files from the Client project's Pages folder:
- Counter.razor
- Weather.razor

Keep Home.razor but rewrite it as a landing page for the shipment tracker.
Keep Auth.razor and NotFound.razor as-is.

### 2. Shared model (in Client project since it needs to be accessible from both)

Create `/tmp/sv-ef500695b1e6440a934dab6536027696/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Delayed
}
```

### 3. Service interface (in Client project)

Create `/tmp/sv-ef500695b1e6440a934dab6536027696/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string customerEmail);
    Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status);
}
```

### 4. Client-side implementation (HttpClient-based, in Client project)

Create `/tmp/sv-ef500695b1e6440a934dab6536027696/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentServiceClient.cs`:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ShipmentServiceClient(HttpClient http) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>("api/shipments") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        return await http.GetFromJsonAsync<Shipment?>($"api/shipments/track/{trackingNumber}");
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string customerEmail)
    {
        return await http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>($"api/shipments/customer/{Uri.EscapeDataString(customerEmail)}") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        await http.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", status);
    }
}
```

### 5. Register HttpClient and service in Client Program.cs

Edit `/tmp/sv-ef500695b1e6440a934dab6536027696/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Program.cs` to:
```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Hosting;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

var builder = WebAssemblyHostBuilder.CreateDefault(args);

builder.Services.AddAuthorizationCore();
builder.Services.AddCascadingAuthenticationState();
builder.Services.AddAuthenticationStateDeserialization();

builder.Services.AddHttpClient("ShipmentTracker.ServerAPI", client =>
    client.BaseAddress = new Uri(builder.HostEnvironment.BaseAddress));
builder.Services.AddScoped(sp => sp.GetRequiredService<IHttpClientFactory>().CreateClient("ShipmentTracker.ServerAPI"));
builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentServiceClient>();

await builder.Build().RunAsync();
